\b WORKING DRAFT\b0\line
This editable Word-compatible handover is AI-assisted and requires student review. It is not evidence of team approval, participant testing, Blackboard submission or achieved carbon reduction.\par
\b 1. Product stage\b0\par
Footprint Lens is a low-fidelity Contextual Choice Coach. It helps a user record one routine, keep scope visible, inspect factor assumptions, receive a feasible non-judgemental action and understand when a factor is unavailable.\par
\b 2. D1 traceability\b0\par
S1 motivates familiar context and provenance; S2 motivates food, packaging, waste and repair/reuse records without unsupported credits; S3 motivates a short/offline path; L1/L2 motivate the shared-total boundary; L3 motivates protected choices. The D1 JTBD remains unchanged.\par
\b 3. Three concepts\b0\par
Concept A — Contextual Choice Coach: activity to transparent result to feasible action.\line
Concept B — Household Commons Board: communal cards, shared discussion and optional consented view.\line
Concept C — Quiet-Week Action Cards: explicit constraints followed by inspectable weekly cards.\par
Concept A is a provisional candidate because it covers E1–E5 in one small route and is feasible for a Java/JavaFX MVP. The choice and novelty claim require genuine team confirmation and verified competitor evidence.\par
\b 4. Prototype\b0\par
P0 entry/scope; P1 quantity and validation; P2 universal result; P3 structured assumptions; P4 action; P5 unavailable estimate; P6 shared total. The interaction inventory is in D2/prototype/INTERACTION-INVENTORY.md.\par
\b 5. Verification\b0\par
Seven pure prototype logic tests passed; the structure contract passed; JavaScript syntax passed; local HTTP asset smoke passed. Browser, keyboard, screen-reader and participant walkthroughs remain human review gates.\par
\b 6. Submission gates\b0\par
Add authentic ideation evidence, final team choice, verified novelty comparison, actual student review, compiled/inspected PDF, exact GenAI disclosure and any required genuine minutes/reviews before formal use.\par
\b 7. References and formatting\b0\par
Use D2/report/main.tex for the formal A4, 12 pt, 1.5 cm source and ACM-style reference section. Team email addresses remain placeholders until supplied.\par
